The rain stopped. The clouds broke apart. Then, I saw it.

It was not just one rainbow. It was two.

The first one was bright and bold. It stretched from the old oak tree to the top of the hill. The red was like a fire truck. The yellow was like a school bus. The blue was like the sky on a clear day. It was perfect.

But then, I looked closer. Above the first one, there was a second rainbow. It was softer. The colours were pale, like watercolours washed in the rain. The red was pink. The blue was light as a feather. It looked like a ghost of the first rainbow.

I stood in the wet grass. My boots were muddy. I did not care. I just watched. The double rainbow shimmered. It felt like a secret. It felt like magic.

I have seen many rainbows. Some are short. Some are faint. But this one, with its twin sister above it, was the best. It made me smile. It made me feel small and happy.

I took a deep breath. The air smelled of wet earth and fresh leaves. I wished I could keep it in a jar. But I knew I couldn’t. So I just remembered it. I closed my eyes and held the image in my mind.

When I opened them, the sun was out. The rainbows were gone. But the feeling stayed. It was a good feeling. A quiet, happy feeling. I walked home, smiling. I knew I would see it again. Maybe tomorrow. Maybe next year. But for now, I had the memory. And that was enough. [end of text]


